  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 528ecde27feefd74eb359b784c14f552, type: 3}
  m_Name: Abby
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::DollConfig
  dollName: Abby
  dollOwner: Jenna Wonder, 18 y.o., female, alive
  dollStory: "Jenna was diagnosed with Antisocial Personality Disorder (ASPD). In
    addition to exhibiting hostile behavior toward her classmates, she also tortured
    and disfigured her doll\u2014ripping out its eye and hair, burning it with a
    blowtorch, and throwing it around. Despite her parents throwing the doll away,
    it mysteriously returned to Jenna's room. On one occasion, she even buried it,
    yet it reappeared without any signs of disturbance at the burial site or dirt
    on its surface. However, the doll stopped returning after Jenna was sent to prison
    for attacking a boy at her high school with a knife, leaving him with a scar
    across his arm. Since then, the doll has remained motionless."
  dollReason: "Abby harbors a neutral spirit. She developed a desire to help Jenna
    with her struggles, although she didn't fully understand where Jenna's problems
    were coming from. Believing that allowing Jenna to release her frustrations and
    anger on her would help, Abby endured the pain\u2014unaware that this spirit
    could actually feel it. Abby tried to reach out to Jenna, but Jenna was too unstable,
    almost like a rabid animal. The boy Jenna stabbed has since recovered, and Jenna
    has been transferred from prison to a psychiatric ward, where she is receiving
    treatment for her severe case of ASPD. Abby has shown herself to be a kind spirit
    who simply couldn't help her best friend with a problem far more complex than
    she anticipated."
